From d5242b96be5b42d0033fa277c6cb77db780583ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sostk <poudelswastik@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:25:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Name the blocking call when the playback thread misses
 its stop deadline

A webOS 4.4.3 tester's log (cloudstream-webos-native issue 15) shows a
playback thread that never came back after its first video frame: stop()
gave up after 2 s and detached it, the decoder was never unloaded, and
every later Load waited 20 s for it. The warning did not say whether the
thread was in a Starfish call, a source call or waiting on the reader.

- media/src/controller.cpp: a Busy marker on the playback thread around
  every backend call (load, feed, unload, pause/play, flush, end of
  stream), source open/seek and the reader park/join; the stop deadline
  warning names it and how long it has been running.
- unload_backend()/pause_backend() helpers carry the marker; steady_ms()
  replaces the repeated steady-clock arithmetic.
- tests/unit/test_media.cpp: the stuck-load test checks the warning says
  "in backend load".

Verified with host tests (test_media 39/39).
