From 2981d49b15f59b6a6599cb175aab71c6b5cdf740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sostk <poudelswastik@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:25:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Report a seek's target as the position until it reaches
 the screen

The position comes from the backend's presented PTS when it has one, so
after a seek it keeps showing the old content: through the source seek,
priming, and on Starfish the backlog the splice plays first. Apps that
draw the time from the snapshot showed the old time for a second or
more after every fast-forward press (cloudstream-webos-native issue 18:
"the timestamp does not update simultaneously").

- media/src/controller.cpp: seek() records the target and a generation
  under the lock; snapshot() reports the target as the position while it
  is set. The playback thread clears it once a packet of that seek went
  in, or with a splicing backend once splice_settled() says it is on
  screen; only for the newest seek, so one still held or queued keeps
  showing. Opening, stopping, failing and a seek with nothing open clear
  it.
- media/include/wnk/media/controller.hpp: documents the position rule.
- tests/unit/test_media.cpp: the target shows at once and, splicing,
  until settled; of two seeks the newer one shows; a seek before open
  leaves nothing behind.

Verified with host tests (tools/test.sh host-debug 111/111) and
ThreadSanitizer (unit.media under host-tsan).
